WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.173
A wave.

00:00:02.173 --> 00:00:04.226
A bird nearby.

00:00:04.226 --> 00:00:06.528
A gap in the traffic.

00:00:06.528 --> 00:00:10.581
SoundWalk gives you one small reason to stop and listen.

00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:15.871
Outdoors, you record five seconds.

00:00:15.871 --> 00:00:19.555
Here, I’m using the credited shoreline sample.

00:00:19.555 --> 00:00:24.410
The open YAMNet model runs in this browser and suggests water.

00:00:26.374 --> 00:00:28.629
You choose what to follow.

00:00:28.629 --> 00:00:34.695
This invitation asks you to pick out one small splash within the larger wash of sound.

00:00:36.646 --> 00:00:39.822
Then the page dims for sixty seconds.

00:00:39.822 --> 00:00:43.072
Read once, look up, and listen.

00:00:43.072 --> 00:00:46.177
This film skips ahead through the minute.

00:00:50.642 --> 00:00:53.949
When you return, write one thing you noticed.

00:00:53.949 --> 00:00:56.502
Here is a scripted example.

00:00:56.502 --> 00:01:01.476
The card keeps the model’s suggestion, your choice, and your words.

00:01:03.834 --> 00:01:07.970
Save an image, or keep your field notes on this device.

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:11.747
After preparation, the model works offline.

00:01:11.747 --> 00:01:15.102
Try SoundWalk, and bring back a sound.

